{%- comment -%}
  theinmag-single-mags-inside
  Inside-gallery section for /products/single-mags. Sits between the
  hero (1) and UGC (2) on the PDP. No direct archetype parent - this
  is a hybrid of audience-tiles full-bleed scroll-rail (6.10) + the
  Membership UGC swipe strip rhythm.

  Layout:
    Desktop: two-zone. Left ~25% is a sticky text panel; right ~75%
    is a horizontal scroll-snap rail of mixed-aspect kid-page samples
    pulled from each issue's `single_mag.inside_gallery_images` list.
    Mobile: heading stacks above, gallery becomes full-bleed swipe.

  Per-issue galleries all in DOM, scoped by [data-issue-handle]. JS
  listens for the `single-mags:issue-changed` event broadcast by the
  hero's picker and swaps the visible container + heading text.

  The heading wraps "INside" with .theinmag-in so the IN reads at
  1.4em per the sitewide brand-pun pattern.

  Imagery sourcing: kid-page samples from the magazine, sharp-cornered,
  no overlays. White-on-cream text panel on the left. No coloured pills
  on photography (per feedback_premium_photo_text memory).
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign issues_collection_handle = section.settings.issues_collection
  assign issues = collections[issues_collection_handle].products
  assign aeo_heading = section.settings.aeo_heading | default: "What's inside theINmag?"
  assign eyebrow = section.settings.eyebrow | default: "you're looking inside"
  assign heading_prefix = section.settings.heading_prefix | default: 'INside'
  assign pad_top = section.settings.padding_top | default: 64
  assign pad_bottom = section.settings.padding_bottom | default: 64

  assign section_style = '--tmsi-pt: ' | append: pad_top | append: 'px; --tmsi-pb: ' | append: pad_bottom | append: 'px;'

  # Sort newest-first to match the hero's initial picker order. The
  # first issue here is the default visible gallery; JS swaps when
  # the picker fires a custom event.
  assign sorted_issues = issues | sort: 'metafields.single_mag.issue_number.value' | reverse

  # Pick which gallery of IMAGES to show on load. The pill LABEL is
  # always the current product's own name (set in the markup below) -
  # so the Digital Stack page reads "Inside Digital Stack" even though
  # the images it shows are borrowed from a magazine.
  #   1. If the current product is itself an issue WITH its own inside
  #      gallery, show that - a mag's own page shows its own pages.
  #   2. Otherwise (Snack Pack, Digital Stack, anything with no gallery)
  #      fall back to the current issue from the theinmag.current_issue
  #      _number shop metafield - a taste of the latest mag.
  #   3. Last resort: newest issue with print in stock, else newest.
  # On the single-mags reference page the picker JS swaps both the
  # gallery and the label via the single-mags:issue-changed event.
  assign initial_issue = nil
  for issue in sorted_issues
    if issue.handle == product.handle
      assign product_inside_images = issue.metafields.single_mag.inside_gallery_images.value
      if product_inside_images != blank
        assign initial_issue = issue
      endif
      break
    endif
  endfor
  if initial_issue == nil
    assign current_issue_mf = shop.metafields.theinmag.current_issue_number.value
    if current_issue_mf != blank
      assign current_issue_handle = current_issue_mf | downcase
      for issue in sorted_issues
        if issue.handle == current_issue_handle
          assign initial_issue = issue
          break
        endif
      endfor
    endif
  endif
  if initial_issue == nil
    assign initial_issue = sorted_issues.first
    for issue in sorted_issues
      if issue.metafields.single_mag.print_in_stock == true
        assign initial_issue = issue
        break
      endif
    endfor
  endif

  assign heading_in_prefix = ''
  assign heading_in_suffix = ''
  if heading_prefix contains 'IN'
    assign heading_in_parts = heading_prefix | split: 'IN'
    assign heading_in_prefix = heading_in_parts[0]
    assign heading_in_suffix = heading_in_parts[1]
  endif
-%}

<section
  id="see-inside"
  class="theinmag-single-mags-inside"
  data-theinmag-single-mags-inside
  aria-labelledby="theinmag-single-mags-inside-heading"
  style="{{ section_style }}"
>
  <h2 id="theinmag-single-mags-inside-heading" class="theinmag-single-mags-inside__a11y-heading">{{ aeo_heading }}</h2>

  {%- comment -%}
    Iteration 4 restructure: dropped the sticky text-panel + horizontal
    rail two-zone layout in favour of a full-bleed swipe strip with a
    single "Inside MagNN" pill overlaid in the top-left corner.
    Visual register mirrors the Membership UGC banner (one pill on a
    full-bleed photo strip) - feels native to the brand rather than
    a fresh template move. JS still listens to the picker event and
    swaps the visible gallery + updates the pill label.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <div class="theinmag-single-mags-inside__rail-wrap">
    <span class="theinmag-single-mags-inside__pill" data-pill aria-hidden="true">
      Inside <span data-issue-label>{{ product.title | default: initial_issue.title | replace: 'theINmag - ', '' | replace: 'theINmag ', '' }}</span>
    </span>

    {%- comment -%}
      Desktop-only prev/next arrows. Marquee auto-scrolls, so the
      buttons pause the loop (via the inline-script `pause()` hook
      stashed on the active rail element), scrollBy ~60% of the
      viewport, then scheduleResume so the marquee picks up again
      after a beat. Single pair targets the currently-visible
      gallery's rail; hidden galleries are unreachable from these.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <button type="button" class="theinmag-single-mags-inside__nav theinmag-single-mags-inside__nav--prev" data-inside-nav="prev" aria-label="Previous inside page">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
        <path d="M15 18l-6-6 6-6"/>
      </svg>
    </button>
    <button type="button" class="theinmag-single-mags-inside__nav theinmag-single-mags-inside__nav--next" data-inside-nav="next" aria-label="Next inside page">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
        <path d="M9 18l6-6-6-6"/>
      </svg>
    </button>

    <div class="theinmag-single-mags-inside__galleries" data-galleries>
      {%- for issue in sorted_issues -%}
        {%- liquid
          assign inside_images = issue.metafields.single_mag.inside_gallery_images.value
          assign is_active_issue = false
          if issue.handle == initial_issue.handle
            assign is_active_issue = true
          endif
        -%}
        <div
          class="theinmag-single-mags-inside__gallery"
          data-issue-handle="{{ issue.handle }}"
          data-gallery
          {% unless is_active_issue %}hidden{% endunless %}
        >
          {%- if inside_images != blank -%}
            {%- comment -%}
              Auto-scrolling marquee, same rhythm as the Membership UGC
              banner and the homepage press band. Items rendered TWICE
              in the track; CSS animates translateX(0) -> translateX(-50%)
              so the second set takes the first set's position exactly
              as the animation completes, creating a seamless loop.
              Pause on hover. Reduced-motion kills the animation +
              re-enables natural overflow scroll.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            <div class="theinmag-single-mags-inside__rail" data-rail>
              <ol class="theinmag-single-mags-inside__rail-track" role="list" data-rail-track>
                {%- for img in inside_images -%}
                  <li class="theinmag-single-mags-inside__rail-item">
                    <img
                      class="theinmag-single-mags-inside__rail-img"
                      src="{{ img | image_url: width: 1400 }}"
                      alt="{{ img.alt | default: issue.title | escape }} - inside page sample"
                      loading="lazy"
                    >
                  </li>
                {%- endfor -%}
                {%- for img in inside_images -%}
                  <li class="theinmag-single-mags-inside__rail-item" aria-hidden="true">
                    <img
                      class="theinmag-single-mags-inside__rail-img"
                      src="{{ img | image_url: width: 1400 }}"
                      alt=""
                      loading="lazy"
                    >
                  </li>
                {%- endfor -%}
              </ol>
            </div>
          {%- endif -%}
        </div>
      {%- endfor -%}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<script>
  (function () {
    'use strict';

    const root = document.querySelector('[data-theinmag-single-mags-inside]');
    if (!root) return;

    const galleries = Array.from(root.querySelectorAll('[data-gallery]'));
    const issueLabel = root.querySelector('[data-issue-label]');

    function setActiveIssue(handle) {
      galleries.forEach(function (g) {
        g.hidden = g.dataset.issueHandle !== handle;
      });
    }

    document.addEventListener('single-mags:issue-changed', function (ev) {
      const detail = ev.detail || {};
      if (!detail.handle) return;
      setActiveIssue(detail.handle);
      const heroMeta = document.querySelector('[data-issues-meta]');
      if (!heroMeta || !issueLabel) return;
      try {
        const all = JSON.parse(heroMeta.textContent);
        const match = all.find(function (m) { return m.handle === detail.handle; });
        if (match && match.title) {
          const label = match.title.replace(/theINmag\s*-?\s*/, '');
          issueLabel.textContent = label;
        }
      } catch (err) { /* swallow */ }
    });

    /* Auto-scrolling marquee with manual override.
       Each rail runs its own RAF loop incrementing scrollLeft at a
       constant rate. User interaction (hover / pointer down / wheel
       / touch) pauses the loop; after a short delay with no
       interaction, the loop resumes. When scrollLeft crosses the
       halfway mark (we render items 2x), JS jumps scrollLeft back by
       half the scrollWidth so the loop is seamless. */
    const reduceMotion = window.matchMedia && window.matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches;
    const speedPxPerSec = 28;
    const resumeDelay = 1500;

    root.querySelectorAll('[data-rail]').forEach(function (rail) {
      const track = rail.querySelector('[data-rail-track]');
      if (!track) return;

      let paused = false;
      let lastTime = 0;
      let resumeTimer = null;

      function loopBack() {
        const half = track.scrollWidth / 2;
        const viewport = rail.clientWidth;
        // No horizontal overflow -> nothing to loop.
        if (half <= 0 || half <= viewport) return;
        // The track holds the strip TWICE, so jumping by exactly `half`
        // lands on the identical frame - invisible. Keep a buffer of slack
        // on BOTH sides of the start so a swipe LEFT has somewhere to go
        // instead of slamming into the scrollLeft=0 wall. (The old code
        // only reset on scrollLeft < 0, which the browser clamps away, so
        // leftward swiping hit a hard stop at the first item.) Symmetric
        // buffer keeps both reset points inside the scrollable range.
        const buffer = (half - viewport) / 2;
        if (rail.scrollLeft >= half + buffer) {
          rail.scrollLeft -= half;
        } else if (rail.scrollLeft < buffer) {
          rail.scrollLeft += half;
        }
      }

      function step(now) {
        if (reduceMotion) return;
        if (!lastTime) lastTime = now;
        const delta = (now - lastTime) / 1000;
        lastTime = now;
        if (!paused) {
          rail.scrollLeft += speedPxPerSec * delta;
          loopBack();
        }
        window.requestAnimationFrame(step);
      }

      function pause() {
        paused = true;
        if (resumeTimer) { window.clearTimeout(resumeTimer); resumeTimer = null; }
      }
      function scheduleResume() {
        if (resumeTimer) window.clearTimeout(resumeTimer);
        resumeTimer = window.setTimeout(function () {
          paused = false;
          lastTime = 0;
        }, resumeDelay);
      }

      // Expose pause/resume on the rail element so the global
      // prev/next nav buttons (rendered once per rail-wrap, not
      // per gallery) can drive the marquee on the active rail.
      rail.theinmagPause = pause;
      rail.theinmagResume = scheduleResume;

      // Pause on cursor over the rail. Resume when the cursor leaves.
      rail.addEventListener('mouseenter', pause);
      rail.addEventListener('mouseleave', scheduleResume);

      // Touch + pointer interactions pause for resumeDelay after release.
      rail.addEventListener('touchstart', pause, { passive: true });
      rail.addEventListener('touchend', scheduleResume, { passive: true });
      rail.addEventListener('pointerdown', pause);
      rail.addEventListener('pointerup', scheduleResume);

      // Wheel scrolling: pause + reschedule resume on every wheel tick.
      rail.addEventListener('wheel', function () { pause(); scheduleResume(); }, { passive: true });

      // Native scroll (from any source) - always loop back if we've
      // crossed the halfway mark, so manual scrolling is also infinite.
      rail.addEventListener('scroll', loopBack, { passive: true });

      // Drag-to-scroll on desktop. Lets users grab + pull the rail.
      let isDragging = false;
      let dragStartX = 0;
      let dragStartScroll = 0;
      rail.addEventListener('mousedown', function (e) {
        isDragging = true;
        dragStartX = e.pageX;
        dragStartScroll = rail.scrollLeft;
        rail.style.cursor = 'grabbing';
        pause();
      });
      window.addEventListener('mousemove', function (e) {
        if (!isDragging) return;
        e.preventDefault();
        rail.scrollLeft = dragStartScroll - (e.pageX - dragStartX);
      });
      window.addEventListener('mouseup', function () {
        if (!isDragging) return;
        isDragging = false;
        rail.style.cursor = '';
        scheduleResume();
      });

      if (reduceMotion) {
        // Auto-scroll is off, so the rail rests where it loads (0). Shift
        // one strip-width in so a left-swipe has a copy to scroll back
        // into. scrollLeft = half shows the same first item as 0 (two
        // identical copies), so the first paint is unchanged. Re-run on
        // window load once lazy images give the rail its real width.
        var positionStart = function () {
          var half = track.scrollWidth / 2;
          if (half > rail.clientWidth) rail.scrollLeft = half;
        };
        positionStart();
        window.addEventListener('load', positionStart);
      } else {
        // Auto-scroll path: loopBack() runs every frame and self-positions
        // from 0 into the buffered band on the first frame (seamless -
        // identical copies), so no explicit start offset is needed here.
        window.requestAnimationFrame(step);
      }
    });

    /* Desktop prev/next nav buttons. One pair lives in the rail-wrap;
       on click we find the visible gallery's rail, drive scrollBy a
       fraction of the viewport, and use the rail's own pause/resume
       hooks so the marquee yields gracefully. Buttons are CSS-hidden
       on mobile - touch users get the swipe gesture. */
    const prevBtn = root.querySelector('[data-inside-nav="prev"]');
    const nextBtn = root.querySelector('[data-inside-nav="next"]');

    function activeRail() {
      const visibleGallery = root.querySelector('[data-gallery]:not([hidden])');
      return visibleGallery ? visibleGallery.querySelector('[data-rail]') : null;
    }

    function navStep(dir) {
      const rail = activeRail();
      if (!rail) return;
      const stepPx = Math.max(280, rail.clientWidth * 0.6);
      if (typeof rail.theinmagPause === 'function') rail.theinmagPause();
      rail.scrollBy({ left: dir * stepPx, behavior: 'smooth' });
      if (typeof rail.theinmagResume === 'function') rail.theinmagResume();
    }

    if (prevBtn) prevBtn.addEventListener('click', function () { navStep(-1); });
    if (nextBtn) nextBtn.addEventListener('click', function () { navStep(1); });
  })();
</script>

{% stylesheet %}
  .theinmag-single-mags-inside {
    background-color: var(--color-cream);
    color: var(--color-inky-purple-navy);
    padding: var(--tmsi-pt, 64px) 0 var(--tmsi-pb, 64px);
    position: relative;
    /* overflow:visible so the centred pill can straddle the section's
       top edge - half over the section above, half over the images.
       The rail keeps its own overflow-x:auto, so nothing else leaks. */
    overflow: visible;
  }

  .theinmag-single-mags-inside__a11y-heading {
    position: absolute;
    width: 1px;
    height: 1px;
    padding: 0;
    margin: -1px;
    overflow: hidden;
    clip: rect(0, 0, 0, 0);
    white-space: nowrap;
    border: 0;
  }

  /* Full-bleed rail wrap. The pill is centred and straddles the wrap's
     top edge - bottom half over the sliding images, top half lifting
     onto the section above, so it reads as a label FOR these pages. */
  .theinmag-single-mags-inside__rail-wrap {
    position: relative;
    width: 100%;
  }

  .theinmag-single-mags-inside__pill {
    position: absolute;
    top: 0;
    left: 50%;
    transform: translate(-50%, -50%);
    z-index: 4;
    background: var(--color-cream);
    color: var(--color-inky-purple-navy);
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: clamp(18px, 2vw, 24px);
    line-height: 1;
    padding: 10px 18px;
    border-radius: 999px;
    box-shadow: 0 4px 16px rgba(42, 31, 61, 0.18);
    font-synthesis: none;
    pointer-events: none;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  /* ---------- Gallery rail (JS-driven scroll) ---------- */
  /* Iteration 8 rewrite: rail is a scrollable overflow-x: auto
     container. JS auto-scrolls scrollLeft each frame at a constant
     speed. User interaction (hover / touch / wheel / pointer drag)
     pauses the auto-scroll, resumes after a delay. Items rendered
     twice in the track; JS jumps scrollLeft back by half the track
     width when it crosses the halfway mark, creating a seamless loop.
     Reduced-motion disables the auto-scroll loop, leaves manual
     scrolling. */
  .theinmag-single-mags-inside__galleries {
    width: 100%;
    min-width: 0;
  }

  .theinmag-single-mags-inside__gallery[hidden] { display: none; }

  .theinmag-single-mags-inside__rail {
    width: 100%;
    overflow-x: auto;
    overflow-y: hidden;
    -webkit-overflow-scrolling: touch;
    scrollbar-width: none;
    scroll-behavior: auto;
  }
  .theinmag-single-mags-inside__rail::-webkit-scrollbar { display: none; }

  .theinmag-single-mags-inside__rail-track {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: nowrap;
    gap: var(--space-md);
    width: max-content;
  }

  .theinmag-single-mags-inside__rail-item {
    flex: 0 0 auto;
  }

  .theinmag-single-mags-inside__rail-img {
    display: block;
    height: clamp(320px, 56vw, 580px);
    width: auto;
    max-width: none;
    object-fit: contain;
    background-color: rgba(251, 246, 234, 0.6);
    box-shadow: 0 8px 24px rgba(42, 31, 61, 0.18);
    border-radius: 0;
    /* Allow the user to drag-scroll across images without the
       browser kicking in image-drag behaviour. */
    user-select: none;
    -webkit-user-drag: none;
    pointer-events: none;
  }

  @media (max-width: 749px) {
    .theinmag-single-mags-inside__pill {
      padding: 8px 14px;
    }
  }

  /* Prev/next nav buttons - desktop only. The marquee auto-scrolls
     and accepts touch swipe + drag on its own; the buttons are an
     extra affordance for mouse + keyboard users. Pinned to the
     rail-wrap edges, vertically centred over the gallery height. */
  .theinmag-single-mags-inside__nav {
    display: none;
  }
  @media (min-width: 990px) {
    .theinmag-single-mags-inside__nav {
      display: inline-flex;
      align-items: center;
      justify-content: center;
      position: absolute;
      top: 50%;
      transform: translateY(-50%);
      width: 44px;
      height: 44px;
      padding: 0;
      border-radius: 50%;
      background: rgba(251, 246, 234, 0.95);
      border: 1.5px solid var(--color-inky-purple-navy);
      color: var(--color-inky-purple-navy);
      box-shadow: 0 6px 20px rgba(42, 31, 61, 0.18);
      cursor: pointer;
      z-index: 6;
      transition: background 0.15s ease, transform 0.15s ease;
    }
    .theinmag-single-mags-inside__nav:hover,
    .theinmag-single-mags-inside__nav:focus-visible {
      background: #ffffff;
      transform: translateY(-50%) scale(1.06);
    }
    .theinmag-single-mags-inside__nav--prev { left: 20px; }
    .theinmag-single-mags-inside__nav--next { right: 20px; }
    .theinmag-single-mags-inside__nav svg {
      width: 20px;
      height: 20px;
    }
  }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .theinmag-single-mags-inside__nav { transition: none; }
    .theinmag-single-mags-inside__nav:hover,
    .theinmag-single-mags-inside__nav:focus-visible {
      transform: translateY(-50%);
    }
  }
{% endstylesheet %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Single mags inside",
  "tag": "section",
  "class": "shopify-section theinmag-single-mags-inside-section",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Inside-gallery rail for /products/single-mags. Listens to the hero's issue picker - swap the gallery when the user picks a different issue. Images come from single_mag.inside_gallery_images on each issue product."
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Copy"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "aeo_heading",
      "label": "Hidden H2 (AEO)",
      "default": "What's inside theINmag?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "eyebrow",
      "label": "Eyebrow (Caveat)",
      "default": "you're looking inside"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "heading_prefix",
      "label": "Heading prefix",
      "default": "INside",
      "info": "If it contains IN, the IN renders with the brand-pun emphasis."
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Per-issue source"
    },
    {
      "type": "collection",
      "id": "issues_collection",
      "label": "Issues collection",
      "info": "Same collection used in the hero. Reads single_mag.inside_gallery_images per product."
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Spacing"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding_top",
      "label": "Padding top",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 128,
      "step": 4,
      "default": 64,
      "unit": "px"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding_bottom",
      "label": "Padding bottom",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 128,
      "step": 4,
      "default": 64,
      "unit": "px"
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    { "name": "Single mags inside" }
  ],
  "enabled_on": {
    "templates": ["product", "page"]
  }
}
{% endschema %}
